  "finalReply": "Created the modernized stack without modifying the legacy code:\n\n**1. `/app/analyze_climate_modern.py`** — Python 3 script that:\n- Uses `pathlib.Path` for file paths (`BASE_DIR / \"climate_analyzer\" / ...`)\n- Reads the CSV with `pd.read_csv(csv_path, encoding=\"utf-8\", parse_dates=[\"date\"])`\n- Reads `config.ini` with modern `configparser.ConfigParser().read(path, encoding=\"utf-8\")`\n- Groups by `station_id` and prints `Station {id} mean temperature: {value:.1f}°C` (sorted, so 101 then 102)\n- Contains no Python 2 syntax (`print()`, `configparser`, no `xrange`/`unicode`/`cPickle`/`urllib2`/deprecated numpy/pandas APIs)\n\n**2. `/app/requirements.txt`** — modern dependency pins with `>=` constraints:\n- `numpy>=1.24`, `pandas>=2.0`, `matplotlib>=3.7`, `scipy>=1.10`\n\nExpected output based on the sample data: `Station 101 mean temperature: -15.5°C` and `Station 102 mean temperature: 30.3°C`.",
